erall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["BPA Music","Strong Theory + Performance","Composition Practice","DAW & Music Production","Film/Game/Commercial Scoring Projects","Composer Assistant/Freelance Work","Professional Composer","Music Producer/Music Director"]},{"type":"p","text":"For maximum employability, the strongest profile is excellent musical fundamentals + distinctive composition style + professional DAW skills + arrangement/orchestration + film/media scoring + mixing awareness + a strong portfolio + collaboration/networking + understanding of music rights and commercial delivery."},{"type":"note","label":"Career-fitment mapping note","text":"Music composition is a highly portfolio- and network-driven profession. A degree provides structured musical training, but professional opportunities depend heavily on the quality of original compositions, production ability, collaboration, credits and industry relationships. By graduation, the student should ideally have a professional demo reel containing original songs, instrumental compositions, film cues, commercial music and at least one complete scored short-film project."}]}]}